  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional advice to the Muttukadu Resilient Waterscapes Project in Chennai</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of this Private Sector Development (PSD) project is to provide advice on the process of developing a Detailed Project Report (DPR) for the Indian Government. This advice is used as input for a Develop2Build (D2B) study and a potential investment via DRIVE. The DPR focuses on a project that addresses flooding and water supply concerns around a Specialized Economic Zone (SIPCOT) outside of Chennai, by revitalising green and blue infrastructures. The project builds on a proposal developed under the &#x201c;Water as Leverage&#x201d; (WaL) program and will connect and re-integrate the upstream forest and water bodies to the urbanising landscape below, by restoring critical ecologies and greening open space.</narrative>
  </description>
